# Sandbox bind-mount artefacts.
#
# When a sandboxed process inside the Claude Code harness attempts to read
# user dotfiles or IDE config that the sandbox blocks, the harness leaves
# behind /dev/null character devices (major 1 minor 3, owned by
# nobody:nogroup) at the corresponding paths in the current working dir.
# Some leak at the repo root, some leak inside any subdir from which a
# sandboxed bash inspected dotfiles. Ignore them so `git status` stays
# meaningful — they are not real files and cannot be deleted by the
# project user.

# Root-level litter (user dotfiles + IDE config).
/.bash_profile
/.bashrc
/.gitconfig
/.gitmodules
/.profile
/.zprofile
/.zshrc
/.ripgreprc
/.mcp.json
/.idea

# .claude/ at root contains real project config (settings.json) but the
# harness creates these three as bind-mount stubs at every .claude/ path
# it touches. They are never legitimate project files at any depth.
**/.claude/agents
**/.claude/commands
**/.claude/skills

# session-2 NKOD recon scratch (oleg-owned files removed in session 3 once
# the findings were absorbed into progress/WP-03-enrolment.md). The dir
# itself can't be deleted while the harness still has devtmpfs bind mounts
# inside its .claude/ subdir.
memory/raw/_scratch/

# Python build / venv detritus.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
.uv-cache/
